/// A program may make a platform of its own: the platform's class is a
/// nested class of the `PlatformFactory` module, whose factory is `new`,
/// and its members reach the module's classes lexically, so a second
/// platform's transcript writes through the mirror the first one's does.
/// The platform hands out the module's classes by methods, `Platform`
/// among them, which makes the second; the collections facet hands out its
/// module's classes as the platform hands out its own. That each answers
/// the class its own members are instances of, which only another object's
/// class would show, `crates/ns-runtime/tests/representation.rs` checks.
class ASecondPlatformWritesLikeTheFirst = Object new () (
  public main: platform args: arguments = (
    |
      second
    |
    second:: platform Platform new.
    platform transcript
        show: 'first';
        newLine.
    second transcript
        show: 'second';
        newLine.
    platform transcript
        show: (second transcript = platform transcript) printString;
        newLine.
    platform transcript
        show: (platform collections Collections new = second collections) printString;
        newLine.
  )
)
